        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "433098",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following list comprehensions in Python will produce a list of numbers from 11 to 49 ?<br> </p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">[i for i in range(100) if i &gt; 10 if i &lt; 50]</pre></li><li><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">[i if i &gt; 11 for i in range(0, 100) if i &lt; 50]\n</pre></li><li><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">[i for i in range(100) if i &gt; 10 and i &lt; 50]</pre></li><li><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">[i if i &gt; 10 else 0 for i in range(100)]\n</pre><p> </p></li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a;c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses2025-python-2,goclasses,python-programming,programming,multiple-selects,one-mark",
          "category": "Programming in Python"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "433106",
          "text": "<p>Consider the following Python code:</p><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">b = [[9,6],[4,5],[7,7]]\n\nx = b[:2]\n\nx[1].append(10)\n</pre><p><br>What will be the contents of the list `b` after executing the code?</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">[[9,6],[4,5],[7,7]]</pre></li><li><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">[[9,6],[4,5,10]]</pre></li><li><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">[[9,6],[4,5,10],[7,7]]\n</pre></li><li><pre data-pbcklang=\"python\" data-pbcktabsize=\"4\" class=\"prettyprint linenums lang-python\">[[9,6],[4,10],[7,7]]</pre></li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2025-python-2,goclasses,python-programming,programming,one-mark",
          "category": "Programming in Python"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "433096",
          "text": "<p>Consider the expression $\\mathrm{x}&gt;=0$ or $\\mathrm{y}&lt;10$. If we assume x is equal to 10 , and y is equal to 5 , then... (hint: think of short-circuit evaluation)</p><ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\"><li>Python will evaluate both conditions in left-right order to determine whether the expression is True.</li><li>Python will evaluate both conditions in right-left order to determine whether the expression is True.</li><li>Python will evaluate only the second condition, $y&lt;10$.</li><li>Python will evaluate only the first condition, $x&gt;=0$.</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2025-python-2,goclasses,python-programming,programming,one-mark",
          "category": "Programming in Python"
        }
